@Override
protected byte[] serializeBytes() {
    writeFrameType();
    writeStreamId();
    long type = frame.getFrameType().getValue();
    if ((type & 0x04) != 0) writeOffset();
    if ((type & 0x02) != 0) writeLength();
    writeData();
    return getAlreadySerialized();
}
```
Note: if LEN is absent, the length field isn't written; data = rest.

Also for the LEN case, should the written length equal data.length? Yes, since the parser read exactly length bytes.

DatagramFrameSerializer: writes length only if isLengthField → good. But if length field present, write `frame.getLength().getValue()` — the parsed length; equals data.length. Fine.

